  "question": {
    "text": "The nature of charge on resulting colloidal particles when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>FeCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> is added to excess of hot water is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "positive",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "sometimes positive and sometimes negative",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "neutral",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "negative",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>FeCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> is added to hot water, a positively charged sol, hydrated ferric oxide is formed due to adsorption of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> ions.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Fe</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#183;</mo><msub><mi>xH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Positively charged.</p><p>Thus,&nbsp;When<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>FeCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>â€‹&nbsp;sol is treated with hot water, it forms&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Fe</mi><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>OH</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#8203;</mo></math>&nbsp;forming&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;ions(in excess amount) and these positive ions are adsorbed preferentially.</p>"
  }
